    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-pŭto</span></b> , āre,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to trim</i> or <i>prune
			thoroughly.</i>—Hence, trop., <i>to set
				forth plainly</i> or <i>neatly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argumentum alicui, ut ego argumentum hoc vobis
					plane perputem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cist. 1, 3, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
